WEBVTT

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.360
All right, let's get ready.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.110
We're entering the mine now.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.400
We should probably assume 
they know we're here, though.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.520
Indeed.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.330
But how'd they find out we were here?

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.050
The enemy's been watching us from above.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.860
The suspicious movements 
of that bird earlier...

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.840
Most likely...

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.770
there's a beast tamer among them.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:47.860
<b>Beast Tamer</b>

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.480
Beast Tamer VS Beast Tamer

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.480
Beast Tamer VS Beast Tamer

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.150
The guys we sent outside 
to check haven't come back.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.910
Think something happened?

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.230
They were beaten.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.820
What do we do?

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.360
We can't afford to be exposed.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.890
We'll crush them!

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.700
Careful, everyone.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:33.560
Runa!

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.230
Yep, this one's on us!

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:39.880
They blocked it?!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.320
One more time!

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.290
We must deflect it.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.010
Yep!

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.220
We'll show Rein just what we can do

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.680
and get more head pats!

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:50.640
What are they doing?!

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.730
They extinguished our spells!

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:56.650
You...

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:57.990
A pointless endeavor!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.130
Truly impressive!

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:04.370
Got 'em down in no time flat!

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.920
Rein, we're all done here!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.560
Sure.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.790
I guess it's down to you.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.980
Damn...

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.440
Just who are you people?

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.750
If I say I'm working for Gantz, 
will that explain it?

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.460
That old bastard?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.280
We've caught you red-handed.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.050
Give yourself up.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:21.950
Shut up!

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.550
You little brat...

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.520
Just turn yourself in.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.680
Damn it...

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.060
I'm not giving up... Not yet...

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.980
Not until I make that old bastard pay!

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.440
Come to me, behemoth!

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.420
What's that sound?

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.490
A behemoth...

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.030
That's a B-rank monster, I believe.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.770
Has he truly tamed a monster?

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.880
Don't they have a natural 
animosity to humans?

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.970
To tame a monster requires many times 
the standard levels of magic power and skill.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.680
You wanna know how I did it?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.930
I found it when it was 
still young and raised it.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.340
So it's got no animosity to me at all.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.890
I didn't need exceptional magic power or skill!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.990
Go, behemoth!

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:16.920
Finish them off!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.280
It's coming!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.920
This seems like a bad sign...

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.780
The entire cave might collapse around us!

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.070
Rein!

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.080
Got it.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.020
We'll take them!

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:35.670
Tania!

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.780
Understood.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.590
Sora, Runa, we're going!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.820
All right!

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.810
Murder him, behemoth!

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.860
I'll watch them.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.980
Thanks, Tania!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.160
Drat.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.620
Get him!

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.910
Are you okay, Rein?

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.370
Yeah, thanks a lot!

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.990
Thank goodness!

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:19.840
Where are the others?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.570
Watching over our prisoners outside.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.180
So I came to help you!

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.940
Let's beat him together!

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.510
No.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.260
I'll fight the behemoth.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.370
While I do, you capture the man.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.900
The behemoth is following his orders.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.190
The fastest way to stop it 
to get him to call it off.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.410
Can you do it?

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.930
Sure thing!

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.740
Strategy meeting all over, eh?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.820
I can't let anyone know 
about our theft of the ore.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.780
Sorry, but I need you to die!

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.090
<i>The behemoth may be strong,</i>

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.300
<i>but it attacks in simple ways.</i>

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.950
<i>Now that I know how it moves,</i>

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:04.050
<i>it won't hit me again.</i>

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.480
<i>But...</i>

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:09.840
<i>The mine won't hold out 
much longer like this!</i>

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.460
Fireball!

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:18.620
<i>That had an effect, 
but I guess it needs to be full-power...</i>

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.310
Rein!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.040
I caught him!

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:21.650
Darn it...

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.930
Great! Hey, call off the behemoth—

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.560
I'd rather die!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.440
Darn it! How come?!

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.100
Sh-Shut up!

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.060
Behemoth!

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.780
Kill that guy!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.070
<i>There's only one way to stop it.</i>

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.520
<i>But can I do it?</i>

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.500
Rein!

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.240
<i>You're not useless at all, Rein!</i>

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:48.220
<i>If anything, you're really strong!</i>

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.200
<i>She said my abilities, 
which I thought were mundane,</i>

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.280
<i>were actually incredibly strong.</i>

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.550
<i>That they were things no one else could do.</i>

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.140
<i>My comrades taught me that.</i>

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.860
<i>I'm going to trust in their words.</i>

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.460
Finish him!

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:06.150
<i>And in my own power!</i>

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.230
Rein!

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.550
What are you doing, behemoth?!

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.180
Beat that guy already!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.320
Darn it... What'd you do to my behemoth?!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.590
I tamed it and took it for my own.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.600
I overwrote your control of the behemoth.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:35.340
What?!

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.930
Overwrote his control?

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:41.400
It would normally be impossible 
to steal control from another tamer.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:45.050
But if I really am as strong 
as my comrades say,

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:47.110
I thought maybe I could do it.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:51.150
<i>To steal control... 
I've never heard of that before.</i>

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.320
<i>Rein really is amazing!</i>

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.520
Preposterous...

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.860
You can't just do that!

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.260
I'm a top-rank beast tamer!

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:02.350
I'm the one who won over the behemoth!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:03.790
Move, behemoth!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.600
I'm your master!

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:06.640
Remember!

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.880
Get him, behemoth!

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.710
Stop! Don't provoke it!

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:12.780
Kill him! Kill him!

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.430
Kill him already!

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.520
Fireball!

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.820
Wh-Why?

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.290
Even through taming,

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.820
it's impossible to fully eliminate 
a monster's animosity towards humans.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.180
It was just barely keeping 
that animosity under control,

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:50.090
but your own animosity sparked it to rampage.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.660
It's a shame, but this was the only way.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:58.360
Rein...

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.180
<i>We talked to the ore thieves.</i>

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:11.730
<i>They had one thing in common: 
they'd all bought weapons from Gantz.</i>

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:16.110
<i>They all bought his 
half-heartedly created weapons.</i>

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.740
<i>But when other adventurers 
pointed out how mediocre they were,</i>

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:23.290
<i>they decided to take revenge</i>

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.660
<i>by stealing the mithril 
so he couldn't make weapons.</i>

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.630
<i>To steal Gantz's pride 
and soul as a craftsman.</i>

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:32.590
So that's the story, eh?

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.900
Gantz...

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.300
How sad.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.440
I put my own weapons on a pedestal,

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.970
and decided the average man 
wasn't worthy to wield them.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:47.820
I should have made them 
all weapons I felt passionate about,

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.440
no matter who they were.

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:50.940
And yet...

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.390
I've been dishonest with both 
my weapons and the customers,

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.900
with those silly tests of mine.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.970
I'm a failure as a craftsman.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:00.660
You might just be.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.490
W-Wait, Rein!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.500
Then make it right.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:07.740
Rein...

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.630
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:14.500
Now that you know you did, you can start 
putting your heart into your weapons again.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:19.200
You have amazing skill and a love of weapons.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.470
I know you can make it right.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:26.680
Can't believe I'm being comforted 
by a boy not even half my age.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.800
Oh, s-sorry.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.100
I shouldn't have lectured...

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.710
No, you've really woken me up!

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:35.150
I'm going to deal honestly with both 
customers and weapons from now on.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.400
I'll make a fresh start,

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.480
and work harder than ever before!

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:42.300
Wow, look at Gantz all cheered up!

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.120
A wonderfully happy ending!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.090
To start, Rein, I'll make your own weapon!

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.830
What kind would you like?

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.530
I'd like a dagger and a gauntlet.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.920
A gauntlet, eh?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:57.440
You sure that's all you want?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.430
Yeah!

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:00.930
And if I can tell you an idea I had...

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:05.040
Well, that's quite an idea!

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:05.850
Right?

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.360
Well, give me some time to get it done.

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:09.480
Sure.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.810
I was just thinking it'd be 
a nice time for a break.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.280
What do you think?

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.020
We're in!

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.480
You fail.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:23.360
No!

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.530
Please, wait a minute.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.880
I meet all the qualifications 
on your recruitment form!

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.420
Why did I fail?!

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.250
Please, tell me!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.300
You say you're a beast tamer...

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.280
But you can only tame 
one animal at once. Correct?

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:41.220
How do you expect to run 
our supply lines like that?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.920
And you, apparently, 
can't fight at all yourself.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:46.880
It's out of the question.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.290
I am a beast tamer!

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:53.290
In battle, I can tame 
something like a bear to fight!

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:55.790
Or a bird, a wolf, or even a monkey!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.080
In that case...

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.650
Can you tame ultimate species?

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:04.840
No one can tame an ultimate species!

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.760
It's absolutely impossible!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:12.300
Which means you're worse than him.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.170
"Him"?

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:15.950
The minimum requirements 
that we're looking for

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.810
is someone who can fight for himself,

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:21.450
as well as provide supply line support.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:24.380
I'm afraid you don't fulfill 
those requirements.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:26.920
Therefore, you fail.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.570
I'll be going, then...

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:33.440
Next.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.650
He was the last one.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.870
What an absolute bust.

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.360
Why is everyone so worthless?

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:43.100
<i>The man he failed just now</i>

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.940
<i>more than met our support role requirements.</i>

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.910
<i>And it wasn't just him.</i>

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:53.910
<i>There were many competent people 
among the new member hopefuls.</i>

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:57.820
<i>He can't help but compare them all to Rein.</i>

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.080
<i>Meanwhile, we're just sitting here, 
our journey forestalled...</i>

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.720
<i>When will we ever defeat the Demon King?</i>

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.160
Excuse me, Arios...

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:11.260
Is it possible your selection 
criteria may be too strict?

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:12.410
Mina,

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.730
are you suggesting my judgment is mistaken?

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.320
C-Certainly not!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:22.410
<i>Now that Rein's gone, he's turning 
his anger on everyone, including me...</i>

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.800
<i>But I have to endure it.</i>

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.860
<i>This is my mission as a servant of God!</i>

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:30.830
<i>Yes... because he is the Hero!</i>

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:35.290
No, your judgment is flawless, of course.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.700
Yeah.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:40.750
I guess we'll just have to hang out 
in this city a little longer.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:45.370
It's possible Leane and Aggath 
might find a good candidate.

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:46.590
You're right.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.720
We mustn't rush things, after all.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.090
Mina, I'm sure you're exhausted 
from all these interviews.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.690
Go on and take a rest.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.240
Thank you.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:01.360
I hope you'll rest when you 
need to, as well, Arios.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:05.760
You have a mission 
to save this world, after all.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:12.240
Save the world, eh?

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.670
There's something I have to do before then.

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.040
Use this...

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:27.210
And eliminate Rein!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.010
Oh?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.410
Hello, Rein!

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.850
Did you come today to see me?

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:40.070
Just had a question, actually.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.810
What happened to those ore thieves earlier?

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:45.440
The ones Gantz hired you to stop?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.430
They were stripped of 
their adventurer licenses

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.910
and sentenced to hard labor.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.490
That's pretty harsh...

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.720
Stealing ore and taming a monster...

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:57.950
Those alone are major crimes, 
but they had other offenses.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.330
It's a suitable punishment.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:01.930
I see...

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.230
Rein!

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:07.500
What did she say?

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.770
The thieves were punished.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:10.680
Rein...

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:15.370
There is no doubt in my mind 
that you behaved correctly.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:19.820
Leaving the behemoth at large would have 
caused great harm to many more people.

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:23.160
Yeah. We got the mithril back, 
and made Gantz happy.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:24.520
It's a good ending!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.630
Sora.

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:26.760
Runa.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:29.240
You're right. Thanks.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:33.240
It's a nice, sunny day.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.650
Want to take a walk before we head back?

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:35.210
Yes!

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.620
Totally!

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.100
This is fun!

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.560
Here you are!

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.640
Rein!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.390
What're those things?!

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.410
Those? They're hot dogs.

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:05.840
Hot dogs?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:06.460
Yeah.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:10.110
Stick a sausage on a bun, 
add ketchup, and eat it.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.320
S-Sausage?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.750
Ketchup?

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:16.780
Want to try one?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:18.030
Hooray!

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.280
Is it good?

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:34.300
Smmgmmmd!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.860
You can tell me when you've finished.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.740
I lost my head and ate it all!

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:43.880
And now it's gone!

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.380
I-If only I had savored it more!

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.480
We can come back here if you like it.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:49.800
Really?!

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.700
Yeah, with Kanade and Tania next time.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.570
Sure!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.570
Of course!

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:57.720
We can rub it in Kanade 
and Tania's faces, too!

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:58.590
Runa...

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.280
Oh, almost forgot!

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.040
We were gonna ask Rein that thing!

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:04.790
What is it?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:10.040
It's about the ability you got 
through contracting with us!

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.090
Ability?

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.730
You attained physical prowess 
by contracting with Kanade.

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.760
You attained greater magic power 
by contracting with Tania.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:20.760
Fireball!

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.560
So contracting with us 
oughta do somethin', too!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.080
Well? Do you feel different in any way?

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.490
Not really, I guess.

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:43.760
Not in the slightest?

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.830
Not even in magic power, 
the fairy specialty?!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.040
Nope.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:55.180
Perhaps he's learned the spells 
in our repertoire!

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:56.880
Yeah! I'll bet!

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.810
Maybe he's got ultimate magic now!

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:02.120
Yes indeed!

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.350
Ultimate magic?

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:04.750
Yeah!

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.050
Way better than advanced and epic magic,

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:10.030
it's a prized technique 
that only us fairies can use!

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.080
Ultimate magic!

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.880
Although we ourselves cannot yet use it...

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:17.200
...maybe you can!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.810
Well?

00:18:18.810 --> 00:18:22.670
Has the structure of the spells 
you learned appeared in your mind?

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:25.660
No, I can't think of any new spells...

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.600
Wh-What's wrong?!

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.680
Our contract has gifted him nothing at all...

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:34.170
I feel like a pair of worthless bums!

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.770
We may be failed familiars!

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.720
Yeah, we're failed familiars!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.380
You're really not!

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.930
I don't judge my companions 
based on contracts and abilities.

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:46.750
Even if you didn't give me anything new,

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:49.390
I still treasure your companionship.

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:52.780
So please, no more talk about being failures.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.720
Hey, Rein.

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:57.610
Why do you put so much faith in us?

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:03.370
Those of our own village abandoned us.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.080
And, I mean, we can't blame them...

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:10.090
Given how bad we messed up, 
it makes sense that they would.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:11.980
Sad though it may be...

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.590
But you do not do the same.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.570
Kanade and Tania are so strong.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.420
The last job showed us that, plain as day.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:22.090
You've got companions 
who are plenty stronger,

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:24.390
but you still act like you need us.

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:26.850
We wanna know why!

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.310
Oh, that?

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.660
I guess I'll tell you, then.

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:36.330
You know I was kicked out of 
the Hero's party, right?

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:39.740
Yes... they fired you without notice.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.930
I've been thinking ever since.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.490
Why didn't that whole thing work out?

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.040
How come?

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:48.360
It wasn't just their fault.

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.470
I didn't trust them, either.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.710
Trust?

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:54.900
Back when we'd first set out,

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:58.140
I didn't have any confidence in myself.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:04.640
Maybe I was afraid of Arios... 
of the Hero telling me that he didn't need me.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.060
So I worked so hard to be useful,

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.200
but they still kicked me out.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.630
Looking back, it was 
a pretty lonely party to be in.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:21.180
But maybe if I'd trusted them more, 
things might have been different.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.000
That's entirely untrue!

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.990
They're totally bad guys!

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.880
Well, there's no changing the past.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:33.330
So now that I've got comrades 
I want to be with,

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.000
I want to work hard to build up trust.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.450
A-And do you see us...

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.200
as comrades, too?

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.550
Yeah! I sure do!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:50.600
You're both my precious comrades.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.650
Even if you don't have a contract ability.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:55.400
I accept your answer, Rein!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.270
Do you, Runa?

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.430
Yep!

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:01.550
Boy, all that tough talk made me hungry!

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:03.150
I wanna go eat!

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.410
But you just ate a hot dog!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.490
But I need more!

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.900
Then, let's call the girls 
and get a proper lunch!

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.260
Agreed!

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:14.510
Let's get goin'!

00:21:14.510 --> 00:21:16.940
You might trip if you don't slow down.

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:20.570
<i>They're back to normal now.</i>

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:21.750
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:24.800
Excuse me. You there.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:33.370
What are your names?

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.690
Wh-Where's this comin' from?!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.420
Tell me at once.

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:39.650
I asked you a question.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:40.910
I-I am Sora.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.020
I-I'm Runa.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:45.240
Sora and Runa, eh?

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:47.570
What fine names.

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:49.870
Decent appearances, as well.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.740
And twins, at that...

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.600
And you seem like worthwhile company.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:58.040
I like you.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:01.860
Yes! I'll deign to make you both mine!

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:03.900
Huh?!

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:40.020
Darkness in Horizon

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:39.270
Next Time: "Darkness in Horizon."
